---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' },
  { label: 'House Clearance Cost Bristol' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the average cost of a house clearance in Bristol?', a: 'The average cost for a 2-3 bedroom house clearance in Bristol is £300–£500. Smaller properties start from £175 and larger 4-5 bed houses typically cost £500–£900. All prices include loading, transport, disposal and a besom clean.' },
  { q: 'Is house clearance cheaper than skip hire in Bristol?', a: 'House clearance is often similar in total cost to skip hire but includes all the labour. Skip hire in Bristol costs £200-350 for the skip alone — you still have to load it yourself. A house clearance service handles everything.' },
  { q: 'Do house clearance companies charge extra for stairs or difficult access?', a: 'Some companies do. At Bristol House Clearances, our quotes include access challenges. We assess access during the quoting process and factor it into the price — so there are no surprises on the day.' },
  { q: 'Can I reduce the cost of a house clearance?', a: 'Yes. Removing items yourself that can go in normal bins, separating items for charity collection, and allowing flexible scheduling can all reduce costs. We\'re happy to advise on the most cost-effective approach.' },
  { q: 'What factors affect house clearance cost?', a: 'The main factors are: property size (number of rooms), volume and weight of items, access difficulty (stairs, narrow doorways, parking), distance from Bristol, and any hazardous materials requiring specialist disposal.' },
];
---

<GuideLayout
  title="House Clearance Cost Bristol 2026 | Prices from £175 — Bristol House Clearances"
  description="How much does house clearance cost in Bristol? Full 2026 pricing guide with tables. From £175 for a 1-bed to £900+ for large properties. Compare options."
  h1="House Clearance Cost in Bristol — 2026 Guide"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  publishDate="2026-01-15"
  updatedDate="2026-03-01"
  readingTime="8 min"
  relatedGuides={[
    { title: 'House Clearance vs Skip Hire', href: '/guides/house-clearance-vs-skip-hire/' },
    { title: 'Clearing a House After Death', href: '/guides/clearing-house-after-death/' },
  ]}
  relatedServices={[
    { title: 'House Clearance', href: '/house-clearance/' },
    { title: 'Probate Clearance', href: '/probate-house-clearance/' },
    { title: 'Furniture Removal', href: '/house-clearance/furniture-removal/' },
  ]}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p>
    <strong>How much does a house clearance cost in Bristol?</strong> In 2026, you can expect to pay between <strong>£175 and £900+</strong> depending on the size of the property, the volume of items, and any access challenges. This guide breaks down every factor that affects pricing and helps you make an informed decision.
  </p>

  <h2>House Clearance Prices in Bristol — Quick Reference</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Property Size</th><th>Typical Price Range</th><th>Average Time</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Studio / bedsit</td><td>£175 – £250</td><td>1-2 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td>1 bed flat</td><td>£200 – £350</td><td>2-3 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2 bed house/flat</td><td>£300 – £450</td><td>3-5 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3 bed house</td><td>£400 – £600</td><td>4-6 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4 bed house</td><td>£500 – £800</td><td>5-8 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5+ bed house</td><td>£700 – £1,200</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hoarder property</td><td>£800 – £2,000+</td><td>1-3 days</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><em>Prices include loading, transport, disposal, Waste Transfer Notes and a besom clean. Correct as of March 2026.</em></p>

  <h2>What Affects the Cost?</h2>

  <h3>1. Property Size and Volume</h3>
  <p>
    The biggest factor is how much there is to clear. A minimally furnished 1-bed flat is obviously quicker and cheaper than a fully furnished 4-bed family home that hasn't been cleared in 30 years. We price by volume, not by room count — so a lightly furnished 4-bed can sometimes cost less than a heavily packed 2-bed.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Access Difficulty</h3>
  <p>
    Bristol's Victorian terraces in areas like <a href="/areas/totterdown/">Totterdown</a>, <a href="/areas/southville/">Southville</a> and <a href="/areas/bedminster/">Bedminster</a> often have narrow hallways, steep stairs and limited parking. <a href="/house-clearance/flat-clearance/">Flat clearances</a> without lifts add labour time. These access challenges can add 10-20% to the price.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Types of Items</h3>
  <p>Standard furniture and household goods are included in normal pricing. Items that can increase cost:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Heavy items</strong> — pianos, safes, cast iron baths</li>
    <li><strong>Hazardous materials</strong> — asbestos, chemicals, oils, paints</li>
    <li><strong>Electrical items</strong> — WEEE disposal regulations apply</li>
    <li><strong>Commercial waste</strong> — different waste classification rules</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. Location and Distance</h3>
  <p>
    Properties within Bristol city (BS1-BS16) are in our core area. Properties in <a href="/areas/bath/">Bath</a>, <a href="/areas/thornbury/">Thornbury</a>, <a href="/areas/clevedon/">Clevedon</a> or other outlying areas may incur a small additional distance charge.
  </p>

  <h3>5. Timing and Urgency</h3>
  <p>
    Same-day and next-day clearances are available at standard rates, subject to availability. There's no urgency premium — but booking a few days ahead gives us the most flexibility.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing by Load Size</h2>
  <p>If you don't need a full property clearance, we also price by load size:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Load Size</th><th>Price</th><th>Equivalent To</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Minimum load</td><td>£50</td><td>A few bags or single small item</td></tr>
      <tr><td>¼ van load</td><td>£120</td><td>Small room or garden tidy</td></tr>
      <tr><td>½ van load</td><td>£200</td><td>1-2 rooms or large garden</td></tr>
      <tr><td>¾ van load</td><td>£320</td><td>Multiple rooms or office</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Full van load</td><td>£400</td><td>Whole property or large clearance</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>House Clearance vs Skip Hire vs Council Bulky Waste</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Option</th><th>Cost (typical)</th><th>Labour</th><th>Speed</th><th>Items Accepted</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>House clearance</td><td>£300–£600</td><td>All included</td><td>Same day</td><td>Everything</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Skip hire (8-yard)</td><td>£250–£350 + permit</td><td>You load it</td><td>3-7 days</td><td>No mattresses, fridges, tyres</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Council bulky waste</td><td>£35/3 items</td><td>You place outside</td><td>2-4 weeks</td><td>Limited items, limited quantity</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    For a more detailed comparison, read our <a href="/guides/house-clearance-vs-skip-hire/">house clearance vs skip hire guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to Get the Best Price</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Send photos</strong> — the more we see, the more accurate the quote</li>
    <li><strong>Be clear about access</strong> — stairs, parking, narrow doors</li>
    <li><strong>Separate personal items first</strong> — reduces the volume we need to handle</li>
    <li><strong>Be flexible on timing</strong> — midweek slots may be cheaper</li>
    <li><strong>Get multiple quotes</strong> — but check they're licensed (we are)</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What's Included in Our Price</h2>
  <p>Every Bristol House Clearances quote includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Full loading and heavy lifting</li>
    <li>Transport to recycling facilities and charity partners</li>
    <li>Responsible disposal and recycling (95%+)</li>
    <li>Waste Transfer Notes (legally required)</li>
    <li>Charity Donation Report</li>
    <li>Besom clean (swept and tidy)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our Price Lock Guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    When we quote a price, that price is <strong>locked</strong>. It will not increase when we arrive — even if there's more to clear than expected. This is our Price Lock Guarantee and it's what sets us apart. Too many customers have been stung by companies that quote low and add charges on the day. We don't do that. Ever.
  </p>

  <h2>Ready to Get a Quote?</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> for a free, no-obligation quote. Send us WhatsApp photos of the property for the fastest response — we typically quote within 2 hours. Or call us on 0117 123 4567.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
